# Iterative Refactoring / Fix Until Done
- When performing code refactors or fixes, check the entire file(s) for errors, syntax issues, or TODOs.
- If issues remain, continue iteratively fixing the code until:
    - No lint errors are present
    - All TODOs are resolved
    - The model outputs "All issues fixed"
- Limit iterations to 10 passes to prevent infinite loops.
- Always return updated code in fenced code blocks or JSON format for safe parsing.
- For multi-file projects or very large files, split content or summarize parts to stay within token limits.
- Keep track of previous iterations to detect if the model is stuck or repeating changes.
- Ensure each iteration only modifies code that needs fixing; do not undo previous valid changes.